1
00:03:42,857 --> 00:03:48,857
Two tiny agents vs. the world's wickedest woman
in a dazzling animated adventure!

2
00:07:25,714 --> 00:07:31,714
The Rescuers is a fantasy, family, animation film
directed by Wolfgang Reitherman.

3
00:11:08,571 --> 00:11:14,571
Two agents of the mouse-run International Rescue Aid Society search for a
little orphan girl kidnapped by sinister treasure hunters.

4
00:14:51,428 --> 00:14:57,428
Bernard (voice), played by Bob Newhart.

5
00:18:34,285 --> 00:18:40,285
Miss Bianca (voice), played by Eva Gabor.

6
00:22:17,142 --> 00:22:23,142
Madame Medusa (voice), played by Geraldine Page.

7
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:06,000
Mr. Snoops (voice), played by Joe Flynn.

8
00:29:42,857 --> 00:29:48,857
Ellie Mae (voice), played by Jeanette Nolan.

9
00:33:25,714 --> 00:33:31,714
Luke (voice), played by Pat Buttram.

10
00:37:08,571 --> 00:37:14,571
The Rescuers is a 1977 American animated adventure comedy-drama film produced by
Walt Disney Productions and released by Buena Vista Distribution.

11
00:40:51,428 --> 00:40:57,428
Bob Newhart and Eva Gabor respectively star as Bernard and Bianca, two mice who are members of the Rescue Aid
Society, an international mouse organization dedicated to helping abduction victims around the world.

12
00:44:34,285 --> 00:44:40,285
Both must free 6-year-old orphan Penny (voiced by Michelle Stacy) from two treasure hunters (played by
Geraldine Page and Joe Flynn), who intend to use her to help them obtain a giant diamond.

13
00:48:17,142 --> 00:48:23,142
The film is based on a series of books by Margery Sharp,
including The Rescuers (1959) and Miss Bianca (1962).

14
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
An early version of The Rescuers entered development in 1962, but was
shelved due to Walt Disney's dislike of its political overtones.

15
00:55:42,857 --> 00:55:48,857
During the 1970s, the film was revived as a project intended for the
younger animators, with the oversight of the senior staff.

16
00:59:25,714 --> 00:59:31,714
Four years were spent on the film's production.

17
01:03:08,571 --> 01:03:14,571
The Rescuers was released on June 22, 1977, to positive critical reception and became a
box office success, earning $48 million during its initial theatrical run.

18
01:06:51,428 --> 01:06:57,428
It has since grossed $169 million after two
theatrical re-releases in 1983 and 1989.

19
01:10:34,285 --> 01:10:40,285
Due to the film's success, a sequel titled The Rescuers Down Under was released in 1990,
which made this the first Disney theatrical animated film to have a sequel.

20
01:14:17,142 --> 01:14:23,142
The film explores themes of rescue, kidnapping, mouse, cartoon, villain.
